hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1326","Yusuf bin Musa and Ahmad bin Uthman bin Hakim al-Awdi narrated to us, they said: Al-Hasan bin Bishr narrated to us - Yusuf said: [he is] Ibn al-Musayyab al-Bajali - and they [both] said: Al-Hakam bin Abd al-Malik narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Salim bin Abi al-Ja'd, from his father, who said: A man met Abdullah [bin Mas'ud] and said: ""Peace be upon you, O Ibn Mas'ud."" Abdullah said: ""Allah and His Messenger have spoken the truth. I heard the Messenger of Allah, upon him be prayer and peace, saying: 'Indeed, among the signs of the Hour is that a man will pass by the mosque without praying two rak'ahs in it, and that a man will not give the greeting of peace except to those he knows, and that the young will make the old feel worthless.'""

Ahmad bin Uthman said: He said: The Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said..."
